@attribute [Route("/components/" + nameof(HxTooltip))]

<ApiDoc Type="typeof(HxTooltip)">
	<MainContent>
		<DocAlert Type="DocAlertType.Warning">
			The tooltip wrapper is rendered only if the <code>Text</code> or <code>WrapperCssClass</code> parameter is set.
			If both are <code>null</code> or empty, only the <code>ChildContent</code> is rendered.
		</DocAlert>

		<DocHeading Title="Basic usage" />
		<Demo Type="typeof(HxTooltip_Demo_BasicUsage)" Tabs="false" />

		<DocHeading Title="HxButton support" />
		<p>The tooltip support is also built-in in the <a href="/components/@nameof(HxButton)">@nameof(HxButton)</a> component via the <code>Tooltip</code> parameter.</p>
		<Demo Type="typeof(HxTooltip_Demo_Button)" Tabs="false" />
		<p>You can use the <a href="/types/@nameof(TooltipSettings)"><code>@nameof(TooltipSettings)</code></a> parameter to customize the tooltip.</p>
		<DocAlert Type="DocAlertType.Info">
			Bootstrap's default tooltip trigger is <code>hover focus</code>, which often keeps the tooltip
			visible after clicking the button since it remains focused. You can change this behavior
			by adjusting the <code>Trigger</code> parameter.<br/>
			To update the default trigger, set <code>HxButton.Defaults.TooltipSettings.Trigger = TooltipTrigger.Hover</code>
			in your application startup.
		</DocAlert>

		<DocHeading Title="Placement" />
		<p>You can change the placement of the tooltip with the <code>@nameof(HxTooltip.Placement)</code> parameter:</p>
		<Demo Type="typeof(HxTooltip_Demo_Placement)" />

		<DocHeading Title="HTML content" />
		<p>Use <code>Html="true"</code> to enable HTML in the tooltip.</p>
		<Demo Type="typeof(HxTooltip_Demo_HtmlContent)" />

		<DocHeading Title="Tooltips on links" />
		<p>Tooltips work on inline elements such as links as well:</p>
		<Demo Type="typeof(HxTooltip_Demo_Links)" Tabs="false" />
		<DocAlert Type="DocAlertType.Info">
			The tooltip wrapper is an inline-block <code>&lt;span&gt;</code>, so a link wrapped in <code>HxTooltip</code> doesn't break across lines.
			Keep the tooltip-enabled links short.
		</DocAlert>

		<DocHeading Title="Custom tooltips" />
		<p>
			You can customize the appearance of tooltips using <a href="/components/HxTooltip#HxTooltip-css-variables">CSS variables</a>.
			Use the <code>@nameof(HxTooltip.CssClass)</code> parameter to add a custom class to the tooltip element and use it to override the local CSS variables.
			In the example below, the custom class maps the tooltip colors to the Bootstrap <code>theme-*</code> variables, so you can combine it with any <code>theme-*</code> class.
		</p>
		<Demo Type="typeof(HxTooltip_Demo_Custom)" />

		<DocHeading Title="Disabled elements" />
		<p>
			Disabled elements use <code>pointer-events: none</code>, so they can't directly receive the events that trigger a tooltip.
			<code>HxTooltip</code> wraps its content in a <code>&lt;span&gt;</code> and attaches the trigger to that wrapper, so a <strong>hover</strong>-triggered tooltip works on disabled elements out of the box&mdash;no extra markup required.
			Focus triggering doesn't apply here, as neither the disabled control nor the wrapper is focusable.
		</p>
		<Demo Type="typeof(HxTooltip_Demo_DisabledElements)" Tabs="false" />

		<DocHeading Title="Programmability" />
		<p>
			You can use the <code>ShowAsync()</code> and <code>HideAsync()</code> methods, as well as the <code>OnShown</code> and <code>OnHidden</code> events,
			to program your own interaction.
		</p>
		<Demo Type="typeof(HxTooltip_Demo_MethodsEvents)" />
		<p>You can also use the <code>DisableAsync()</code> and <code>EnableAsync()</code> methods to control the tooltip behavior.</p>
		<Demo Type="typeof(HxTooltip_Demo_EnableDisable)" />
	</MainContent>
	<CssVariables>
		<ApiDocCssVariable Name="--bs-tooltip-zindex" Default="var(--bs-z-tooltip)">
			Z-index of the tooltip.
		</ApiDocCssVariable>
		<ApiDocCssVariable Name="--bs-tooltip-max-width" Default="200px">
			Maximum width of the tooltip.
		</ApiDocCssVariable>
		<ApiDocCssVariable Name="--bs-tooltip-padding-x" Default="var(--bs-spacer-3)">
			Horizontal padding of the tooltip.
		</ApiDocCssVariable>
		<ApiDocCssVariable Name="--bs-tooltip-padding-y" Default="calc(var(--bs-spacer) * .375)">
			Vertical padding of the tooltip.
		</ApiDocCssVariable>
		<ApiDocCssVariable Name="--bs-tooltip-font-size" Default="var(--bs-font-size-sm)">
			Font size of the tooltip.
		</ApiDocCssVariable>
		<ApiDocCssVariable Name="--bs-tooltip-color" Default="var(--bs-bg-body)">
			Text color of the tooltip.
		</ApiDocCssVariable>
		<ApiDocCssVariable Name="--bs-tooltip-bg" Default="var(--bs-fg-body)">
			Background color of the tooltip (and its arrow).
		</ApiDocCssVariable>
		<ApiDocCssVariable Name="--bs-tooltip-border-radius" Default="var(--bs-radius-5)">
			Border radius of the tooltip.
		</ApiDocCssVariable>
		<ApiDocCssVariable Name="--bs-tooltip-opacity" Default=".95">
			Opacity of the shown tooltip.
		</ApiDocCssVariable>
		<ApiDocCssVariable Name="--bs-tooltip-arrow-width" Default=".8rem">
			Width of the tooltip arrow.
		</ApiDocCssVariable>
		<ApiDocCssVariable Name="--bs-tooltip-arrow-height" Default=".4rem">
			Height of the tooltip arrow.
		</ApiDocCssVariable>
		<ApiDocCssVariable Name="--bs-tooltip-transition-property" Default="opacity">
			CSS property animated when the tooltip is shown or hidden.
		</ApiDocCssVariable>
		<ApiDocCssVariable Name="--bs-tooltip-transition-duration" Default=".15s">
			Duration of the show/hide transition.
		</ApiDocCssVariable>
		<ApiDocCssVariable Name="--bs-tooltip-transition-timing" Default="linear">
			Timing function of the show/hide transition.
		</ApiDocCssVariable>
	</CssVariables>
</ApiDoc>
